What is actually linked
-----------------------

This list is not guessed: it comes from the linker map of the release build
(-Wl,-Map). Besides dale's own code, the binary is built from:

  - llama.cpp: libllama.a, libggml.a, libggml-base.a and libggml-cpu.a
    (CPU backend only; no GPU backends, no network code, no OpenMP).
    Inside libggml-cpu.a, sgemm.cpp (tinyBLAS) and ops.cpp (YaRN) carry
    their own notices, reproduced below.
  - nlohmann/json, from llama.cpp's vendor/ directory. It is header-only,
    so its code is compiled into dale's own object files.
  - GCC 13 runtime, linked statically (-static-libstdc++ -static-libgcc):
    libstdc++.a, libgcc.a, libgcc_eh.a and the crtbeginS.o / crtendS.o
    startup files.
  - glibc, linked dynamically (libc.so.6, libm.so.6, libpthread.so.0,
    libdl.so.2, ld-linux-x86-64.so.2), plus its small startup objects
    (crti.o, crtn.o, libc_nonshared.a). glibc itself is provided by the
    user's system.

Nothing else from llama.cpp's vendor/ directory is linked (no cpp-httplib,
miniaudio, stb, subprocess.h or the hash libraries).


